  "notes": "⛔ **The one entry in this batch with real chord changes, and it is the fastest.** The research calls it full P-Funk harmony — dominant-7 and 9th vamps, clav/Rhodes voicings, \"more harmonic motion than any other entry in this section\" — so this is the only model here that reaches five chords, weights Mixolydian first, and puts `harmonicRhythm` on `1_per_bar` above everything else, while `extensions.triad` falls to 0.2, the lowest in the batch. At 96–108 it is closer to funk tempo than g-funk tempo, which is the research's own framing. ⚠ **The documented rule — \"drums are programmed last… that's how I figure out where to put the kick and the snare\" — is authored as a kit that follows the bass and keys rather than a grid**: the densest and most syncopated kick here (`syncopation` 0.66, `offbeat8thShare` 0.46), the loosest quantize of the LA/Oakland group at 0.75, and live percussion on four lanes. The bass is the groove's leading voice: highly syncopated, melodic, with rests, so `followRootsProb` is 0.32 and `anticipationProb` the highest at 0.45. ⚠ `medium` on the research's high-medium. INFERRED: the specific families — \"dominant-7 and 9th vamps\" and \"real chord changes\" name a vocabulary, not progressions, so the four moving families are the P-Funk default inside that description. The documented layer order (loop → turntable transform → played chords) has no generator and is not modelled. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 50 to 49 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 50 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1. ⚠ **The 1-bar phrase length was removed** (was [4,2,1], now [4,2]). A one-bar phrase looped four times carries less entropy than a four-bar phrase, and it is the countermelody it strangles hardest: a counter answers *inside* the melody’s phrase, so a one-bar shape leaves it nowhere to go. Every worst offender on `counter.rs` carried it. ⛔ The previous session recorded this exact mistake and it arrived again from the other direction — distinctness is combinatorial in the shape LENGTH, not in the option count.",
